### Variables
@base = http://localhost:8080/api

### 1. Register a patient
POST {{base}}/patients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Anita",
  "lastName": "Sharma",
  "mobile": "9876543210",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-01-15",
  "gender": "FEMALE"
}

### 2. Register another patient (for queue ordering demos)
POST {{base}}/patients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Ravi",
  "lastName": "Kumar",
  "mobile": "9123456780",
  "dateOfBirth": "1985-06-20",
  "gender": "MALE"
}

### 3. Duplicate mobile -> 409
POST {{base}}/patients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Anita",
  "lastName": "Sharma",
  "mobile": "9876543210",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-01-15",
  "gender": "FEMALE"
}

### 4. Validation failure -> 400 (bad mobile + future DOB)
POST {{base}}/patients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Bad",
  "lastName": "Data",
  "mobile": "12345",
  "dateOfBirth": "2099-01-01",
  "gender": "OTHER"
}

### 5. Search patients
GET {{base}}/patients?search=anita

### 6. List all patients (empty search)
GET {{base}}/patients

### 7. Add patient to queue (ROUTINE) — replace patientId
POST {{base}}/visits
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patientId": 1,
  "priority": "ROUTINE"
}

### 8. Add second patient as URGENT — replace patientId
POST {{base}}/visits
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patientId": 2,
  "priority": "URGENT"
}

### 9. Second WAITING visit for same patient -> 409
POST {{base}}/visits
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patientId": 1,
  "priority": "ROUTINE"
}

### 10. View waiting queue (URGENT first, then oldest)
GET {{base}}/queue

### 11. Complete a visit — replace id
PATCH {{base}}/visits/1/complete

### 12. Complete again -> 409
PATCH {{base}}/visits/1/complete
